# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# fire-watch — deployment configuration
#
# THIS FILE IS FOR LOCAL DEPLOYS ONLY (`./scripts/create-secrets.sh`).
# The same values also live in the GitHub repository, TWICE — once per
# Environment, because lab and prod must not share a broker password:
#
#   Settings → Environments → lab   → Environment variables / secrets
#   Settings → Environments → prod  → Environment variables / secrets
#
#   Variables (plaintext):  NAMESPACE AMQP_HOST AMQP_PORT DFLY_MASTER_NAME AMQP_USER
#   Secrets   (masked):     AMQP_PASS DRAGONFLY_PASSWORD FW_INGEST_TOKEN KUBECONFIG_B64
#
# NAMESPACE must match the overlay's hard-coded namespace: `fire-watch-lab` for
# k8s/overlays/lab/*, `fire-watch` for k8s/base and k8s/overlays/ghcr.
#
# This template never contains real values. To deploy locally:
#   cp .env.example .env      # fill in
#   ./scripts/create-secrets.sh
#
# .gitignore covers `.env`, `.env.*` and `*.env`. Verify with:
#   git check-ignore -v .env
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [variable] namespace to deploy into. Not created by the manifests.
# lab:  fire-watch-lab       prod: fire-watch
NAMESPACE=fire-watch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RabbitMQ — Secret `fire-watch-rabbitmq` {username,password}
#
# This is the ONLY account: definitions.json deliberately contains no users, so
# RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER/PASS is what creates it on first boot.
#
# AMQP_USER is a VARIABLE, not a secret: it is an account name, not a credential.
# Generate a password with:
#   openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -dc 'A-Za-z0-9' | cut -c1-32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [variable]
AMQP_USER=fw
# [secret]
AMQP_PASS=__GENERATE__

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dragonfly — Secret `fire-watch-dragonfly` {password}
#
# Used by: dragonfly --requirepass, every sentinel `auth-pass`, workers,
# ws-gateway, sentinel-bridge, redis-exporter.
#
# 32 alphanumeric chars, deliberately NOT base64: this value is substituted into
# sentinel.conf with sed, and a `/` in a base64 string would either break the
# substitution or produce a config redis cannot parse.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [secret]
DRAGONFLY_PASSWORD=__GENERATE__

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP ingress — Secret `fire-watch-ingress` {token}
#
# Sent by producers as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [secret]
FW_INGEST_TOKEN=__GENERATE__

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-secrets. Also stored as repository variables so the deploy workflow can
# read them without a secret round-trip.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [variable]
AMQP_HOST=rabbitmq.fire-watch.svc.cluster.local
# [variable]
AMQP_PORT=5672
# [variable]
DFLY_MASTER_NAME=fire-watch-dragonfly

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub-only: not used by a local deploy, so it has no value here.
#
#   KUBECONFIG_B64  base64 of the kubeconfig for the target cluster.
#                   `base64 -w0 < ~/.kube/config` (Linux) or
#                   `base64 -i ~/.kube/config` (macOS)
#
# Stored base64-encoded so a multi-line YAML kubeconfig survives the secret
# field intact; the workflow decodes it to a 0600 file at deploy time.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

